SUMMARY:Applied Mathematics Seminar: Baoli Hao — What Can Ionic Transport
  Data Reveal About Steric Interactions?
LOCATION:GP 346\, The University of Alabama\, Tuscaloosa\, Alabama
DESCRIPTION:Baoli Hao\, Ph.D. candidate in Applied Mathematics\, Illinois I
 nstitute of Technology\nWhat Can Ionic Transport Data Reveal About Steric 
 Interactions?\nTo what extent can microscopic interactions be inferred fro
 m observable dynamics? We investigate this question in ionic transport\, w
 here steric interactions may operate at scales beyond experimental resolut
 ion. Within a unified energy-dissipation framework\, we develop a hierarch
 y of local\, higher-order\, and nonlocal constitutive models to investigat
 e what can be learned from dynamical observations. By connecting interacti
 on scales and observational information with identifiability\, model stabi
 lity\, and predictive accuracy\, we determine the level of constitutive co
 mplexity supported by the data. Our study highlights the distinction betwe
 en recovering microscopic interactions and identifying their observable dy
 namical effects\, providing a general perspective on data-driven coarse-gr
 aining and the limits of learning multiscale physics from finite-resolutio
 n observations.\nhttps://jiazhaomath.github.io/seminar/2026-2027.html#2026
 -10-09
URL:https://jiazhaomath.github.io/seminar/2026-2027.html#2026-10-09
